    {
      "speaker": "Felicjan Janus Twardowski",
      "content": "<div class=\"beyond20-message\"><div class=\"beyond20-header\"><img class=\"beyond20-character-avatar\" src=\"https://www.dndbeyond.com/avatars/51436/558/1581111423-114940824.jpeg?width=150&amp;height=150&amp;fit=crop&amp;quality=95&amp;auto=webp\" title=\"Joyous Wand of Color\" width=\"37\" height=\"37\" /><details open><summary><a>Joyous Wand of Color</a></summary><table><tbody><tr><td><i>Wand, Common</i></td></tr></tbody></table><div class=\"beyond20-description\"><br />This crystalline, prismatic wand can channel the illustrative intent of its wielder. While holding the wand, you can magically create a stroke of color in the air, allowing you to draw in midair or on any surface the wand touches. The effect is illusory, visibly magical, radiates dim light out to 5 feet, and dissipates after 1 hour.<br />If you attempt to draw on an object held or worn by a hostile creature, that creature must succeed on a DC 10 Dexterity saving throw in order to avoid it.<br /></div></details></div></div>",
      "timestamp": "2025-11-17T18:47:31.193Z"
    },
